  "body": "**Blocked by:** #130\n\n## Context\n\nThe user decision must have one database source of truth and must not resume an already completed agent turn.\n\n## Task\n\nAdd authenticated-user approve and reject actions using one atomic `UPDATE ... WHERE id=? AND status='pending'`. Rejection creates no job. Approval atomically records `approved`, `decidedAt`, `decidedBy` and enqueues reserved `approvalExecute` with the request id. The handler reloads the stored payload and performs only that deferred choke-point call, recording the outcome in the audit trail; it creates no AgentSession, reconstructs no conversation, and injects no message into the originating run. Repeated decisions are deterministic no-ops. Keep pending requests indefinitely. Design the handler/store boundary so #89 can add snapshot conflict and exactly-once transaction semantics without replacing the user-facing state machine.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Atomic decisions, approval-only enqueue, deferred call, audit outcome, and authorization hook.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Chat decisions, expiry, notification delivery channels, sandboxing, and #89 evolution.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Concurrent approve/reject yields exactly one winning decision.\n- Rejected requests never execute.\n- Approved execution does not alter/reopen the source run.\n- Retry cannot create a second decision transition.\n",
